{
  "manufacturer": "Fronius",
  "manufacturer_slug": "fronius",
  "model": "Fronius Smart Meter via Datamanager (SunSpec meter model int+SF)",
  "model_slug": "smart-meter-datamanager-sunspec-int-sf",
  "short_model": "Fronius Smart Meter int+SF",
  "aliases": [
    "Fronius Smart Meter 63A",
    "Fronius Smart Meter 50kA",
    "Fronius Smart Meter TS",
    "SunSpec meter model 201/202/203"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "An energy meter wired to a Fronius Datamanager (or Hybridmanager) over Modbus RTU and republished by it, with SunSpec Model Type set to int+SF (meter model 201/202/203).",
  "summary": "When a Fronius Smart Meter is connected to the Datamanager's RS485 port, the Datamanager republishes its readings as a SunSpec device at Modbus unit ID 240 (meter address 1) to 244. With the int+SF data type the meter appears as SunSpec model 201, 202 or 203 after the common block. This map covers the common block, the 16-bit current, voltage, frequency, power and power-factor values with their scale factors, and the end block.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Fronius numbers registers from 1 (SunSpec base register 40001) and tells you to request the register number minus one, so register 40072 is read at wire address 40071. The manual's RTU example reads register 40005 with address bytes 9C 44 (40004)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "Register map archive version 1.1.7-0 (Meter_Register_Map_Int&SF_v1.0.xlsx); manual 42,0410,2049 rev. 033-24022026.",
  "source": {
    "title": "Fronius Datamanager Modbus TCP & RTU (operating instructions) + Meter_Register_Map_Int&SF_v1.0.xlsx",
    "doc_number": "42,0410,2049 (033-24022026)",
    "revision_date": "2026-02",
    "url": "https://www.fronius.com/en/~/downloads/Solar%20Energy/Operating%20Instructions/42,0410,2049.pdf",
    "pages": "PDF English part: printed p. 66 (device IDs 240-244 for meters), printed p. 98 (Meter Model, meter-location sign table); register table = XLSX 'Complete Map' sheet in https://www.fronius.com/en/~/downloads/Solar%20Energy/Operating%20Instructions/SE_EI_Modbus_Sunspec_Maps_State_Codes_Events_EN.zip"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Register table comes from Fronius' official 'Meter_Register_Map_Int&SF_v1.0.xlsx' in the Modbus SunSpec maps ZIP published next to the PDF; behaviour and device IDs come from the PDF.",
    "Addresses assume SunSpec Model Type = int+SF. With the default float setting the meter shows model 211/212/213 and the register layout is different.",
    "Word order: neither the PDF nor the XLSX states the order of 32-bit values, so the 32-bit SID (40001-40002), all acc32 energy counters (TotWhExp 40108, TotWhImp 40116, TotVAhExp 40125, TotVAhImp 40133 and the per-phase/VArh counters, most of which the XLSX marks unsupported) and the 32-bit event field (40175) are left out, together with their energy scale-factor registers.",
    "Phase B/C values are only meaningful on a three-phase meter (model 203).",
    "The sign of W and the meaning of the import/export energy counters depend on the meter location set in the Datamanager (0 grid, 1 load, 3 external generator, 256-511 sub-load); see the location table in the PDF.",
    "The PDF says unsupported int16 values read 0x8000 and unsupported scale factors read 0x8000."
  ],
